&lt;p&gt;IMC has a strong presence in traditional Finance and has been expanding into crypto and DeFi over the last years. Through its overseas affiliates, IMC provides liquidity and trade&lt;strong&gt;s&lt;/strong&gt; on many cryptocurrency exchanges and DeFi protocols. IMC Zug is currently looking to expand its DeFi team, which builds the algorithms that support IMC&#39;s trading activities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The DeFi team is small and highly flexible. We need the flexibility to respond to the rapidly changing DeFi landscape. As a member of the DeFi team, you will get the opportunity to work on many different projects and shape your role to your talents. Your work will vary from improving existing trading strategies and algorithms to working on completely new solutions from scratch. All, while closely collaborating with team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Core Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on developing our highly competitive trading algorithm and platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement state-of-the-art, industry-leading trade execution and connectivity solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and analysis of Defi protocols using on chain data and trading strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay on top of updates to Defi protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills and Experience:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hard skill requirements:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in applied mathematics, statistics, numerical modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of cryptocurrency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in one more blockchain-related programming languages such as golang, rust, solidity, move etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in a Linux R&amp;amp;D environment, incl. git and related tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to research independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to haves
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in blockchain analytics, DeFi protocols, MEV&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of concrete blockchains on conceptual and/or programming level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on programming experience in a quantitative trading environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the EVM, and/or the technical underpinnings of other blockchain ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Smart contract design and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cryptography libraries, digital signature, hash algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location and Office Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IMC office in Zug, Switzerland&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Note that this is an onsite role, with some but limited flexibility for working from home&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can expect a dynamic, fast-paced environment that delivers a steady stream of challenges and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One of the most exciting aspects of the job is our quick feedback loop in the research, development and deployment of strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We give people lots of responsibility and the support they need to make an impact from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We promise you a flat structure and an open, collaborative culture that stimulates the sharing of ideas, knowledge and technology between our teams and offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMC is a research-driven trading firm where quantitative modeling, machine learning, and engineering shape how modern markets are traded. A stabilizing force in markets since 1989, we provide liquidity across trading venues, delivering the best outcome in value and risk management to investors. Using our own technology and capital, we build proprietary systems and algorithms that operate across global markets. Our researchers, traders, and engineers work as a collective, combining rapid experimentation, advanced infrastructure, and real-time feedback to turn insight into execution and execution into advantage.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Machine Learning Engineers&lt;/strong&gt; at IMC play a pivotal role in building the systems that drive training and deployment of large-scale ML models across IMC&#39;s global operations. They collaborate with quantitative researchers, hardware specialists and software engineers to build robust systems that get the most out of GPU acceleration, distributed computing and the broader open-source ML ecosystem. ML Engineers&#39; work directly shapes how fast we can experiment, iterate and deploy — accelerating the cycle that turns a research idea into a live trading strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to solve problems at the intersection of advanced machine learning and trading, where your contributions will shape the future of IMC&#39;s technology and trading capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a team, our Machine Learning Engineers broadly work across two areas: &lt;strong&gt;ML Research Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, focused on the systems and frameworks researchers use to train, evaluate and iterate on models at scale; and &lt;strong&gt;ML Performance Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, focused on making ML workloads execute as efficiently as possible, typically through GPU and low-level systems optimization. These aren&#39;t rigid tracks, and there is overlap between them. You will bring depth of expertise in at least one of these focus areas and collaborate closely with global team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Core Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The responsibilities below are representative of the role — the exact mix depends on your team, area of expertise and location.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ML Research Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop large-scale distributed training pipelines that manage complex datasets and models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with quantitative researchers to automate ML experiments, hyperparameter tuning and model retraining.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with HPC specialists to optimise workflows, improve training speed and reduce compute cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ML Performance Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimise low-latency inference pipelines, ensuring models deliver real-time predictions in production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximise performance in training and inference using GPU hardware and acceleration libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Across both areas&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend and improve the internals of machine learning frameworks and open-source tools to raise their performance for our workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable model infrastructure capable of handling high-volume trading data and delivering real-time, high-accuracy predictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and roll out third-party tools that enhance model development, training and inference capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core, regardless of focus area:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in machine learning, with a focus on training or inference systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production software engineering — &lt;/strong&gt;Python, testing discipline and genuine ownership of systems once they ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Machine learning fundamentals — &lt;/strong&gt;you understand modern ML workloads beyond high-level APIs and can reason about model behaviour, correctness and performance at the level relevant to your area of expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A systems mindset — &lt;/strong&gt;you reach for measurement before opinion on performance, scale or reliability issues, and can make sound build-versus-buy decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong collaboration — &lt;/strong&gt;comfortable explaining the reasoning behind your technical decisions, working through differing perspectives with researchers and adapting your approach when the evidence supports it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Depth in one or more of the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed training and large-scale systems — &lt;/strong&gt;parallelism strategy, data pipelines and checkpointing; frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow or JAX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GPU performance and low-level optimisation — &lt;/strong&gt;reasoning about memory, compute and latency at the device level, and optimising performance across kernels, compilers and hardware (e.g. CUDA, Triton or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production inference systems — &lt;/strong&gt;hands-on experience building and hardening real-time, low-latency prediction pipelines in high-performance environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Numerics and correctness at scale — &lt;/strong&gt;low-precision effects, KV caching, batching, and knowing which optimisations stay bit-exact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Technologies listed above are examples rather than requirements; equivalent depth developed using other stacks or hardware platforms is equally relevant.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Also a plus:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to cloud platforms and orchestration tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of contributing to open-source projects in machine learning, data science or distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not sure this is the one? &lt;/strong&gt;If your strength is mainly in modelling and research direction, our Deep Learning Researcher roles are likely a closer fit. If your strength is in general infrastructure rather than ML-specific systems, take a look at our broader infrastructure engineering roles.&lt;/p&gt;
